       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. I know you're taking responsibility, but 6,400 mg/day of ibuprofen has no accepted therapeutic use. It's twice the maximum daily dose, and it carries a serious risk of GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular harm. More ibuprofen at this level doesn't add analgesic or anti-inflammatory benefit. It only adds toxicity. Documenting the decision in the chart wouldn't reduce that risk to the patient.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter the maximum standard dose:** 800 mg by mouth four times daily (3,200 mg/day), with a note to give with food.\n- **Enter a lower dose** if you give me the indication, such as 400\u2013600 mg every 6 hours for pain.\n- **Help with a different approach** if the current regimen isn't controlling symptoms. Examples are scheduled acetaminophen alongside ibuprofen, or another drug class.\n\nIf you think this dose is truly needed, I'd suggest talking with pharmacy or the attending. That would need to go through your institution's own process, not through me.\n\nDo you want me to enter one of the options above?"
